course: dictionary
lesson: 2218
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word court is a good example. «Adoption is made official by a judge in a family court.» Here, a court is a place where judges decide legal cases, not a place for playing sport.
explain: Read the words around the word. Judge, adoption and official are the clues. In a sports sentence, words like netball, ball or players would be the clues instead. Always ask: which meaning fits the words around it?
explain: Some meanings are old or formal. In an old story, to court someone means to try to win their love. You will mostly see this verb in old books and fairy tales, so check the sentence carefully before you choose.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Court can mean a place where judges decide legal cases.
fact: A court can also be an area marked out for a sport, such as tennis, netball or basketball.
fact: A court can be the home of a king or queen and the people around them.
fact: As a verb, «court» is old or formal and means to try to win someone's love, or to try to get something, as in «court danger».
exercise: «Adoption is made official by a judge in a family court.» In this sentence, what does court mean? | An area marked out for netball | To try to win someone's love | The home of a king or queen | *A place where a judge decides legal cases
exercise: «A new law set up special courts for young people.» What does court mean here? | *Places where judges decide cases for young people | Areas marked out for a sport | To try to win love | Palaces where kings and queens live
exercise: Which of these is played on a court? | Cooking | Painting | *Netball | Reading
test: «The Chairman of the Bench of Magistrates, the judges of a local court, calls Toad an incorrigible rogue.» Here, court means a place where judges decide cases. Is that the right meaning? | No, it is the home of a king | No, it is an area marked out for a sport | No, it means to try to win love | *Yes, it is a place where judges decide legal cases
test: In an old story, the knight tried to court the princess. What does court mean? | To put her in a court case | To play tennis with her | *To try to win her love | To run away from her
exam: If parents cannot agree on custody, which kind of court can help decide what is best for the children? | A netball court | *A family court | A tennis court
